.TH COMMAND * 2019-11-27 "SequoiaDB" "Sequoiadb Method's Manual"
.ad l.ll 72.ce 1000
\fBdb.collectionspace.collection.createIdIndex()\fR
.ce 0
.sp 2

.SH "NAME"

.sp 2
createIdIndex - Create the $id index.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp 2

.sp 2

.sp 2
db.collectionspace.collection.createIdIndex(\fB<options>\fR)
.SH "CATEGORY"

.sp 2

.sp 2
Collection
.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.sp 2
Create the $id index.
.sp 2
\fBoptions (Json Object)\fR
.br
       Attributes to be modified.
.sp 2
       \fBSortBufferSize\fR
.br
              The size of sort buffer used when creating index. 
              And it means don't use sort buffer when the size is zero. 
              The unit is MB and default size is 64MB.
.br
.br
              SortBufferSize:<int32>
.sp 2

.SH "Examples"

.sp 2
Create the $id index with default parameters.
.sp 2
db.foo.bar.createIdIndex()
.sp 2
Specify sort cache size when creating the $id index.
.sp 2
db.foo.bar.createIdIndex( { SortBufferSize: 128 } )